      "documentation": "Java method: closeBigViewers",
      "javadoc_description": "Closes any tethered `Bvv`/`Bdv` viewer(s), if open. Unlike `resetUI()`, this does not touch the loaded image or paths: closing a big-viewer *window* isn't data loss the way clearing paths is (the underlying `PathAndFillManager` is untouched), so this needs no confirmation and is safe to call unconditionally - e.g. from `DemoRunner` before loading a new demo, so a viewer left over from a previous one is never silently orphaned (see `AbstractBigViewer`/`setBvvOnEDT`'s `windowClosing` handler for what \"orphaned\" means here).",
      "category": "Visualization",
      "deprecated": false,
      "since_version": null,
