      "documentation": "Java method: registerActiveCmdWorker",
      "javadoc_description": "Registers (or clears, if `worker` is `null`) the `SwingWorker` currently executing a long-running `CommonDynamicCmd`. Unlike commands launched via `DynamicCmdRunner`, these keep running on their own background thread long after the initiating dialog has closed and `currentState` has reverted to whatever it was before the dialog opened, so they cannot rely on the switch inside `abortCurrentOperation()`. Cancellation is not forcible: the running code must itself poll `Thread.isInterrupted()` (see `AbstractGWDTTracer`'s hot loops) for this to have any effect.",
      "category": "Utilities",
      "deprecated": false,
      "since_version": null,
      "see_also": [],
      "examples": []
    },
